---
import ContentPage from "../components/ContentPage.astro";
---

<ContentPage
	title="FAQ | PAN Card Photo Resizer Online"
	description="Answers about PAN card photo size in KB, signature resizing, 50 KB JPEG exports, privacy, and using the online PAN image resizer."
	canonicalUrl="https://nsdlphotoresize.com/faq/"
	eyebrow="Help and answers"
	heading="PAN card photo resizer frequently asked questions"
	intro="Find quick answers about resizing PAN card photos and signatures, output dimensions, JPEG size limits, privacy, and portal requirements."
>
	<div class="divide-y divide-hairline border-y border-hairline">
		<details class="faq-item">
			<summary>How do I resize a photo for a PAN card?</summary>
			<p>
				Select a photo in the online tool, choose Photograph mode, set
				the dimensions specified by your application, adjust the crop,
				and download the JPEG after reviewing the preview.
			</p>
		</details>
		<details class="faq-item">
			<summary>What is the PAN card photo size in KB?</summary>
			<p>
				File-size requirements depend on the application service and
				can change. This tool targets JPEG files under 50 KB for both
				photo and signature exports, but confirm the current limit on
				the official portal before uploading.
			</p>
		</details>
		<details class="faq-item">
			<summary>Can I resize a PAN card signature to under 50 KB?</summary>
			<p>
				Yes. Select Signature mode to crop and export a signature JPEG.
				The tool targets under 50 KB and reports when an image cannot
				reach the limit at its minimum quality setting.
			</p>
		</details>
		<details class="faq-item">
			<summary>What are the default photo and signature dimensions?</summary>
			<p>
				The editable starting dimensions are 2.5 × 3.5 cm for a photo
				and 4.5 × 2 cm for a signature. Requirements may differ, so use
				the latest instructions from your application portal.
			</p>
		</details>
		<details class="faq-item">
			<summary>Does this work for NSDL and UTI applications?</summary>
			<p>
				This independent image utility can help with an NSDL photo
				resize or UTI photo resize workflow, including photo and
				signature cropping. It is not affiliated with Protean, NSDL, or
				UTIITSL. Check the official portal for its current file rules.
			</p>
		</details>
		<details class="faq-item">
			<summary>Are my images uploaded or stored?</summary>
			<p>
				No. Image selection, crop preview, and export run in your
				browser. Your files are not uploaded to this website, and the
				original image is not overwritten.
			</p>
		</details>
		<details class="faq-item">
			<summary>Does resizing guarantee that my PAN application is accepted?</summary>
			<p>
				No. This tool prepares image files but cannot confirm the
				application’s full requirements or guarantee acceptance. Verify
				the final image and all other application details on the
				official service before submitting.
			</p>
		</details>
	</div>
	<p>
		<a class="text-link" href="/how-it-works/">Read the step-by-step guide</a>
		<span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>
		<a class="text-link" href="/#photo-tool">Open the PAN card photo resizer</a>
	</p>
</ContentPage>
